WEBVTT

00:00.700 --> 00:03.766
Every tablet has a batch. And an expiry
date.

00:05.117 --> 00:10.680
Most retail software treats medicine like
groceries. A pharmacy can't run on that.

00:10.833 --> 00:15.274
PharmaFlow is one platform for the
counter, the stockroom and the books.

00:16.117 --> 00:21.734
The till is built for a queue. Every line
shows the batch and expiry the customer is

00:29.800 --> 00:36.066
An urgent customer arrives mid-order? Open
a new tab. The first basket stays exactly

00:36.066 --> 00:38.964
And when the internet drops, the counter
keeps selling.

00:41.133 --> 00:46.957
Stock isn't a number. Every row is a
batch, and the till reaches for the one

00:49.383 --> 00:53.443
A slow mover warns six months out. A fast
one, thirty days.

00:53.443 --> 00:57.290
Drop in a distributor's price list. It
becomes your catalogue.

00:57.483 --> 01:03.015
Profit means one thing everywhere. Revenue
after tax, cost from the batch that sold.

01:03.433 --> 01:06.888
An audit that reads your records and can
never change them.

01:09.883 --> 01:14.276
And across every pharmacy: what each one
trades, and which have gone quiet.

01:14.533 --> 01:19.030
Fifteen hundred tests. A hundred and nine
tables. Ten pipelines.

01:20.150 --> 01:22.970
Schema to C.I. Till to A.I. Let's talk.
